Rem ==================================================================
Rem xml.shoddy — Shoddy standard library: XML 1.0, well-formed
Rem
Rem A reader and a writer, pure Shoddy. A node is an Xml:
Rem
Rem     XDocument | XElem | XText | XComment | XPI | XCData | XDoctype
Rem
Rem An element's attributes are a List Of Pair — name in Fst, value in
Rem Snd — which is precisely dict.shoddy's association list, so DictGet,
Rem DictPut and friends work on them unchanged and XAttr/XPutAttr are
Rem thin wrappers rather than a second implementation.
Rem
Rem     Let doc  = XmlParse(ReadFile("feed.xml"))
Rem     Let ttl  = XFind(XRoot(doc), "title")
Rem     Print(XTextOf(ttl))
Rem     Print(XAttrOr(XRoot(doc), "version", "1.0"))
Rem     Print(XmlPretty(doc, 2))
Rem
Rem The reader returns a WHOLE DOCUMENT, not the root element: the XML
Rem declaration, any comments and processing instructions around the
Rem root, the doctype and the whitespace between them are all kept, so
Rem what went in can come back out. XRoot reaches the root element,
Rem which is what most programs actually want.
Rem
Rem The guard-pair convention, the same shape as json's and as str's
Rem Bool/BoolOr: the strict word is the one you reach for first, and the
Rem total word is there the moment the input stops being yours.
Rem
Rem     XmlParse / XmlRead        XAttr / XAttrOr    XChild / XChildOr
Rem     XFind / XFindOr           XPath / XPathOr    XRoot / XRootOr
Rem
Rem Shoddy has no catchable errors, so a parser that could only abort
Rem would be untestable on malformed input and unusable on untrusted
Rem input. XmlRead is therefore total: it returns XOk or XErr, and XErr
Rem carries the reason and the 1-based offset where the parse gave up.
Rem
Rem ---- known limits ------------------------------------------------
Rem
Rem Well-formed XML only. This is not a validating parser: a DOCTYPE is
Rem carried through as one opaque node and its internal subset is never
Rem read, so a document that declares its own entities is rejected with
Rem UNKNOWN ENTITY rather than silently losing them.
Rem
Rem The five predefined entities and numeric character references, and
Rem nothing else. &amp; &lt; &gt; &quot; &apos; &#NN; and &#xNN;. NUL
Rem cannot be carried — Chr(0) is the empty string in Shoddy — so &#0;
Rem is rejected rather than silently dropped, which would hand back a
Rem string shorter than the document said it was.
Rem
Rem Text is decoded, so a round trip is CANONICAL rather than literal.
Rem &#65; comes back as A and a single-quoted attribute comes back
Rem double-quoted. What the writer guarantees is that it is a fixed
Rem point: parse-write-parse-write agrees byte for byte from the first
Rem write on, and XmlText(XmlParse(x)) = x exactly when x is already in
Rem that canonical form. XmlCanonical goes further and sorts attributes
Rem by name, recursively, for anyone who needs a stable ordering.
Rem
Rem Namespaces are not resolved. A prefixed name is carried literally,
Rem prefix and all, and xmlns attributes are ordinary attributes.
Rem XPrefix and XLocal split a name when you need the halves; mapping a
Rem prefix to a URI is the caller's business.
Rem
Rem The encoding declaration is advisory. ReadFile decides how the bytes
Rem became a string long before this machine sees them, so a document
Rem that says UTF-16 and arrives as UTF-8 is read as it arrived.
Rem
Rem Whitespace is preserved exactly, including between elements, because
Rem in XML it may be significant and nothing here can tell when it is.
Rem XmlPretty re-indents an element only when none of its children is
Rem text or CDATA. Mixed content and anything holding a CDATA section go
Rem out exactly as XmlText would write them, because a line break added
Rem inside either one changes what the document says.
Rem
Rem Compare with XEqual, not with =. A List is a quotation and compares
Rem by identity, so two structurally identical elements are not = each
Rem other. XEqual is the deep comparison.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "dict.shoddy"
Include "str.shoddy"

Type Xml = XDocument(XNodes As List Of Xml) | XElem(XTag As String, XAttrs As List Of Pair, XKids As List Of Xml) | XText(XChars As String) | XComment(XBody As String) | XPI(XTarget As String, XData As String) | XCData(XRaw As String) | XDoctype(XDtd As String)

Rem The public result of a total parse.
Type XRead = XOk(XTree As Xml) | XErr(XWhy As String, XAt As Number)

Rem The internal one, threaded through the whole recursive descent: every
Rem step returns its node AND the 1-based index of the next unconsumed
Rem character, or why and where it gave up.
Type XTake = XTook(XTVal As Xml, XTNext As Number) | XTBad(XTWhy As String, XTAt As Number)

Rem ---- constants -------------------------------------------------------
Rem Machines cannot carry a top-level Let, so the constants are zero-arg
Rem Defs, as vt100's Esc() is.

Def XQt() As String
    Chr(34)

Def XAp() As String
    Chr(39)

Def XNl() As String
    Chr(10)

Rem Deep enough for any document a person wrote, shallow enough that a
Rem hostile one cannot exhaust the stack. Same budget json uses.
Def XmlMaxDepth() As Number
    200

Rem The longest entity name worth looking for. &quot; is the longest of
Rem the five; a numeric reference to the top of the plane is &#1114111;.
Def XEntMax() As Number
    12

Rem ======================================================================
Rem THE READER
Rem ======================================================================

Rem The five characters XML calls whitespace.
Def XIsWs(c As String) As Boolean
    c = " " Or c = Chr(9) Or c = XNl() Or c = Chr(13)

Def XSkipWs(s As String, i As Number) As Number
    If i > Len(s) Then
        i
    Else
        If XIsWs(Mid(s, i, 1)) Then
            XSkipWs(s, i + 1)
        Else
            i

Def XIsDigit(c As String) As Boolean
    c >= "0" And c <= "9"

Rem str's Trim takes spaces off the ends and NOTHING ELSE — not tabs, not
Rem newlines, not carriage returns. Markup is mostly made of those three,
Rem so the two questions this machine actually asks about whitespace get
Rem their own words rather than a Trim that would quietly answer no.
Def XIsBlank(s As String) As Boolean
    XSkipWs(s, 1) > Len(s)

Def XTrimWs(s As String) As String
    If Len(s) = 0 Then
        s
    Else
        If XIsWs(Left(s, 1)) Then
            XTrimWs(Mid(s, 2, Len(s)))
        Else
            If XIsWs(Right(s, 1)) Then
                XTrimWs(Left(s, Len(s) - 1))
            Else
                s

Rem A name may start with a letter, an underscore or a colon. Everything
Rem at or above 128 is admitted rather than spelling out the several
Rem thousand code points XML actually permits — the effect is that a
Rem name with an accent in it is accepted, which is the right answer for
Rem every document that has one.
Def XIsNameStart(c As String) As Boolean
    If Len(c) <> 1 Then
        False
    Else
        (Asc(c) >= 65 And Asc(c) <= 90) Or (Asc(c) >= 97 And Asc(c) <= 122) Or c = "_" Or c = ":" Or Asc(c) >= 128

Def XIsNameChar(c As String) As Boolean
    If Len(c) <> 1 Then
        False
    Else
        XIsNameStart(c) Or XIsDigit(c) Or c = "-" Or c = "."

Rem The index just past the name at i. Self-tail-recursive, so it
Rem compiles to a loop and a long name costs no stack.
Def XNameEnd(s As String, i As Number) As Number
    If XIsNameChar(Mid(s, i, 1)) Then
        XNameEnd(s, i + 1)
    Else
        i

Rem ---- entities --------------------------------------------------------
Rem The five XML predefines, plus numeric references in either base.
Rem Anything else is an error here: resolving it would need the internal
Rem subset this machine deliberately does not read.

Rem The index of the semicolon closing the reference at i, or 0.
Def XSemiFrom(s As String, i As Number, last As Number) As Number
    If i > last Or i > Len(s) Then
        0
    Else
        If Mid(s, i, 1) = ";" Then
            i
        Else
            XSemiFrom(s, i + 1, last)

Def XEntEnd(s As String, i As Number) As Number
    XSemiFrom(s, i + 1, i + XEntMax())

Rem The name between & and ;, without either.
Def XEntName(s As String, i As Number) As String
    Let e = XEntEnd(s, i)
    If e = 0 Then
        ""
    Else
        Mid(s, i + 1, e - i - 1)

Rem The text one of the five stands for, or "" if it is not one of them.
Def XEntNamed(name As String) As String
    Select Case name
        Case "amp"
            "&"
        Case "lt"
            "<"
        Case "gt"
            ">"
        Case "quot"
            XQt()
        Case "apos"
            XAp()
        Case Else
            ""

Def XIsDigits(t As String) As Boolean
    If Len(t) = 0 Then
        False
    Else
        All(Map(Range(1, Len(t)), Fn(k) => Mid(t, k, 1)), XIsDigit)

Def XHexVal(c As String) As Number
    If XIsDigit(c) Then
        Asc(c) - 48
    Else
        If c >= "a" And c <= "f" Then
            Asc(c) - 87
        Else
            If c >= "A" And c <= "F" Then
                Asc(c) - 55
            Else
                0 - 1

Def XIsHexes(t As String) As Boolean
    If Len(t) = 0 Then
        False
    Else
        All(Map(Range(1, Len(t)), Fn(k) => XHexVal(Mid(t, k, 1))), Fn(v) => v >= 0)

Def XHexOf(t As String) As Number
    Fold(Map(Range(1, Len(t)), Fn(k) => XHexVal(Mid(t, k, 1))), 0, Fn(acc, v) => acc * 16 + v)

Rem The code point a numeric reference names, or -1 if the name is not a
Rem well-formed numeric reference at all.
Def XEntCode(name As String) As Number
    If Left(name, 2) = "#x" Or Left(name, 2) = "#X" Then
        If XIsHexes(Mid(name, 3, Len(name) - 2)) Then
            XHexOf(Mid(name, 3, Len(name) - 2))
        Else
            0 - 1
    Else
        If Left(name, 1) = "#" Then
            If XIsDigits(Mid(name, 2, Len(name) - 1)) Then
                Val(Mid(name, 2, Len(name) - 1))
            Else
                0 - 1
        Else
            0 - 1

Rem How many characters the reference at i occupies, or 0 if what is
Rem there is not a reference this machine can resolve. i points AT the &.
Def XEntLen(s As String, i As Number) As Number
    Let e = XEntEnd(s, i)
    If e = 0 Then
        0
    Else
        Let name = XEntName(s, i)
        If XEntNamed(name) <> "" Or XEntCode(name) > 0 Then
            e - i + 1
        Else
            0

Rem A code point as its UTF-8 BYTES, one per character.
Rem
Rem This is the load-bearing decision in the whole machine, and it comes
Rem from the runtime rather than from XML. ReadFile is Latin-1: one byte
Rem in the file is one character in the string, which is what lets the
Rem same words read a PNG. So an em dash sitting literally in a UTF-8
Rem document arrives as the three characters 226 128 148 — and if this
Rem decoded &#8212; to Chr(8212) instead, the same character written two
Rem ways would give two different strings, XEqual would say they differ,
Rem and WriteFile would turn the second into a question mark, because a
Rem character above 255 has no byte to be written as.
Rem
Rem Encoding to UTF-8 here means the entity and the literal agree, and
Rem what comes out is a valid UTF-8 file again.
Def XUtf8(n As Number) As String
    If n < 128 Then
        Chr(n)
    Else
        If n < 2048 Then
            Chr(192 + Fix(n / 64)) & Chr(128 + (n Mod 64))
        Else
            If n < 65536 Then
                Chr(224 + Fix(n / 4096)) & Chr(128 + (Fix(n / 64) Mod 64)) & Chr(128 + (n Mod 64))
            Else
                Chr(240 + Fix(n / 262144)) & Chr(128 + (Fix(n / 4096) Mod 64)) & Chr(128 + (Fix(n / 64) Mod 64)) & Chr(128 + (n Mod 64))

Rem The text the reference at i stands for. Only ever called when
Rem XEntLen said there was one.
Def XEntText(s As String, i As Number) As String
    Let name = XEntName(s, i)
    If XEntNamed(name) <> "" Then
        XEntNamed(name)
    Else
        XUtf8(XEntCode(name))

Rem Why the reference at i is not one we can resolve. Only ever called
Rem when XEntLen said it was not.
Def XEntWhy(s As String, i As Number) As String
    Let e = XEntEnd(s, i)
    If e = 0 Then
        "UNTERMINATED ENTITY REFERENCE — NO ; WITHIN " & Str(XEntMax()) & " CHARACTERS"
    Else
        Let name = XEntName(s, i)
        If XEntCode(name) = 0 Then
            "&#0; IS NOT REPRESENTABLE — A SHODDY STRING CANNOT CARRY NUL"
        Else
            If Left(name, 1) = "#" Then
                "MALFORMED NUMERIC CHARACTER REFERENCE &" & name & ";"
            Else
                "UNKNOWN ENTITY &" & name & "; — ONLY amp lt gt quot apos AND NUMERIC REFERENCES ARE RESOLVED"

Rem ---- text runs -------------------------------------------------------
Rem The scanner tracks the start of the current undecoded RUN so ordinary
Rem text — the overwhelming case — costs one fragment rather than one per
Rem character. Flush the run [run, i) onto the fragment list if non-empty.

Def XRun(s As String, run As Number, i As Number, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    If i > run Then
        Prepend(Mid(s, run, i - run), acc)
    Else
        acc

Rem Character data up to the next < or the end of the document. Returns
Rem the decoded text and where it stopped. Never called with i past the
Rem end, and never returns an empty run.
Def XTextAt(s As String, i As Number) As XTake
    XTextBody(s, i, i, { })

Def XTextBody(s As String, i As Number, run As Number, acc As List Of String) As XTake
    If i > Len(s) Then
        XTook(XText(Join(Reverse(XRun(s, run, i, acc)), "")), i)
    Else
        Let c = Mid(s, i, 1)
        If c = "<" Then
            XTook(XText(Join(Reverse(XRun(s, run, i, acc)), "")), i)
        Else
            If c = "&" Then
                If XEntLen(s, i) = 0 Then
                    XTBad(XEntWhy(s, i), i)
                Else
                    XTextBody(s, i + XEntLen(s, i), i + XEntLen(s, i), Prepend(XEntText(s, i), XRun(s, run, i, acc)))
            Else
                XTextBody(s, i + 1, run, acc)

Rem ---- comments, PIs, CDATA, doctype -----------------------------------
Rem Each of these is a hunt for a fixed closing delimiter.

Rem Instr always searches from the beginning, so searching from i means
Rem searching the tail and adding the offset back. The tail is copied,
Rem which is why this is used for the four fixed delimiters below and
Rem never inside a per-character loop.
Def XInstrFrom(s As String, i As Number, sub As String) As Number
    If i > Len(s) Then
        0
    Else
        Let p = Instr(Mid(s, i, Len(s) - i + 1), sub)
        If p = 0 Then
            0
        Else
            i + p - 1

Def XCommentAt(s As String, i As Number) As XTake
    Let e = XInstrFrom(s, i + 4, "-->")
    If e = 0 Then
        XTBad("UNTERMINATED COMMENT", i)
    Else
        XTook(XComment(Mid(s, i + 4, e - i - 4)), e + 3)

Def XCDataAt(s As String, i As Number) As XTake
    Let e = XInstrFrom(s, i + 9, "]]>")
    If e = 0 Then
        XTBad("UNTERMINATED CDATA SECTION", i)
    Else
        XTook(XCData(Mid(s, i + 9, e - i - 9)), e + 3)

Rem <?target data?>, with the data allowed to be empty. The target is a
Rem name; everything to ?> after one space is the data, verbatim.
Def XPIAt(s As String, i As Number) As XTake
    Let n = XNameEnd(s, i + 2)
    If n = i + 2 Then
        XTBad("EXPECTED A NAME AFTER <?", i)
    Else
        Let e = XInstrFrom(s, n, "?>")
        If e = 0 Then
            XTBad("UNTERMINATED PROCESSING INSTRUCTION", i)
        Else
            XTook(XPI(Mid(s, i + 2, n - i - 2), XTrimWs(Mid(s, n, e - n))), e + 2)

Rem The doctype is carried whole and never read. An internal subset in
Rem square brackets may itself contain a >, so the scan steps over a
Rem bracketed section before looking for the closing angle.
Def XDoctypeAt(s As String, i As Number) As XTake
    Let b = XInstrFrom(s, i + 9, "[")
    Let e = XInstrFrom(s, i + 9, ">")
    If e = 0 Then
        XTBad("UNTERMINATED DOCTYPE", i)
    Else
        If b > 0 And b < e Then
            Let c = XInstrFrom(s, b, "]")
            If c = 0 Then
                XTBad("UNTERMINATED DOCTYPE INTERNAL SUBSET", i)
            Else
                Let f = XInstrFrom(s, c, ">")
                If f = 0 Then
                    XTBad("UNTERMINATED DOCTYPE", i)
                Else
                    XTook(XDoctype(Mid(s, i + 9, f - i - 9)), f + 1)
        Else
            XTook(XDoctype(Mid(s, i + 9, e - i - 9)), e + 1)

Rem ---- attributes ------------------------------------------------------

Rem An attribute value, from its opening quote, decoded. Either quote
Rem character may delimit it; the other is then ordinary text.
Def XAttrValue(s As String, i As Number) As XTake
    XAttrBody(s, i + 1, i + 1, Mid(s, i, 1), { })

Def XAttrBody(s As String, i As Number, run As Number, q As String, acc As List Of String) As XTake
    If i > Len(s) Then
        XTBad("UNTERMINATED ATTRIBUTE VALUE", i)
    Else
        Let c = Mid(s, i, 1)
        If c = q Then
            XTook(XText(Join(Reverse(XRun(s, run, i, acc)), "")), i + 1)
        Else
            If c = "<" Then
                XTBad("A RAW < IS NOT ALLOWED IN AN ATTRIBUTE VALUE", i)
            Else
                If c = "&" Then
                    If XEntLen(s, i) = 0 Then
                        XTBad(XEntWhy(s, i), i)
                    Else
                        XAttrBody(s, i + XEntLen(s, i), i + XEntLen(s, i), q, Prepend(XEntText(s, i), XRun(s, run, i, acc)))
                Else
                    XAttrBody(s, i + 1, run, q, acc)

Rem The attribute list of a start tag, gathered until > or />. Returns
Rem the attributes as an element with no children and no name, which is
Rem the only way to hand a List Of Pair back through an XTake.
Def XAttrsAt(s As String, i As Number, acc As List Of Pair) As XTake
    Let k = XSkipWs(s, i)
    If k > Len(s) Then
        XTBad("UNTERMINATED START TAG", k)
    Else
        Let c = Mid(s, k, 1)
        If c = ">" Or Mid(s, k, 2) = "/>" Then
            XTook(XElem("", Reverse(acc), { }), k)
        Else
            If Not XIsNameStart(c) Then
                XTBad("EXPECTED AN ATTRIBUTE NAME, > OR /> IN A START TAG", k)
            Else
                Let n = XNameEnd(s, k)
                Let name = Mid(s, k, n - k)
                Let eq = XSkipWs(s, n)
                If Mid(s, eq, 1) <> "=" Then
                    XTBad("EXPECTED = AFTER THE ATTRIBUTE " & name, eq)
                Else
                    Let v = XSkipWs(s, eq + 1)
                    If Mid(s, v, 1) <> XQt() And Mid(s, v, 1) <> XAp() Then
                        XTBad("AN ATTRIBUTE VALUE MUST BE QUOTED", v)
                    Else
                        If DictHas(acc, name) Then
                            XTBad("DUPLICATE ATTRIBUTE " & name, k)
                        Else
                            Select Case XAttrValue(s, v)
                                Case XTBad(why, at)
                                    XTBad(why, at)
                                Case XTook(XText(val), n2)
                                    XAttrsAt(s, n2, Prepend(Pair(name, val), acc))
                                Case Else
                                    XTBad("EXPECTED AN ATTRIBUTE VALUE", v)

Rem ---- elements --------------------------------------------------------
Rem Elements and their children are genuinely mutually recursive and so
Rem consume stack in proportion to NESTING DEPTH, which is small for real
Rem documents and unbounded on adversarial input — hence the depth budget
Rem d, spent one level at a time. The child loop, by contrast, calls only
Rem itself in tail position, so a wide element costs no stack at all.

Def XElemAt(s As String, i As Number, d As Number) As XTake
    If d <= 0 Then
        XTBad("NESTING TOO DEEP", i)
    Else
        Let n = XNameEnd(s, i + 1)
        If n = i + 1 Then
            XTBad("EXPECTED AN ELEMENT NAME AFTER <", i)
        Else
            Let tag = Mid(s, i + 1, n - i - 1)
            Select Case XAttrsAt(s, n, { })
                Case XTBad(why, at)
                    XTBad(why, at)
                Case XTook(XElem(ignored, attrs, kids0), k)
                    If Mid(s, k, 2) = "/>" Then
                        XTook(XElem(tag, attrs, { }), k + 2)
                    Else
                        XKidsAt(s, k + 1, d, tag, attrs, { })
                Case Else
                    XTBad("EXPECTED A START TAG", i)

Rem The children of an open element, up to and including its end tag.
Def XKidsAt(s As String, i As Number, d As Number, tag As String, attrs As List Of Pair, acc As List Of Xml) As XTake
    If i > Len(s) Then
        XTBad("UNTERMINATED ELEMENT <" & tag & ">", i)
    Else
        If Mid(s, i, 2) = "</" Then
            Let n = XNameEnd(s, i + 2)
            Let close = Mid(s, i + 2, n - i - 2)
            If close <> tag Then
                XTBad("</" & close & "> CLOSES <" & tag & ">", i)
            Else
                Let e = XSkipWs(s, n)
                If Mid(s, e, 1) <> ">" Then
                    XTBad("EXPECTED > TO CLOSE </" & tag, e)
                Else
                    XTook(XElem(tag, attrs, Reverse(acc)), e + 1)
        Else
            Select Case XNodeAt(s, i, d - 1)
                Case XTBad(why, at)
                    XTBad(why, at)
                Case XTook(v, n)
                    XKidsAt(s, n, d, tag, attrs, Prepend(v, acc))
                Case Else
                    XTBad("EXPECTED CONTENT OR AN END TAG IN <" & tag & ">", i)

Rem One node: an element, a comment, a PI, a CDATA section, or a run of
Rem character data. Not an end tag — the child loop deals with those.
Def XNodeAt(s As String, i As Number, d As Number) As XTake
    If Mid(s, i, 1) <> "<" Then
        XTextAt(s, i)
    Else
        If Mid(s, i, 4) = "<!--" Then
            XCommentAt(s, i)
        Else
            If Mid(s, i, 9) = "<![CDATA[" Then
                XCDataAt(s, i)
            Else
                If Mid(s, i, 9) = "<!DOCTYPE" Then
                    XDoctypeAt(s, i)
                Else
                    If Mid(s, i, 2) = "<?" Then
                        XPIAt(s, i)
                    Else
                        If Mid(s, i, 2) = "</" Then
                            XTBad("UNEXPECTED END TAG", i)
                        Else
                            XElemAt(s, i, d)

Rem ---- the document ----------------------------------------------------
Rem Top level: any number of comments, PIs, doctypes and runs of
Rem whitespace, with exactly one element among them.

Def XDocNodes(s As String, i As Number, d As Number, roots As Number, acc As List Of Xml) As XRead
    If i > Len(s) Then
        If roots = 1 Then
            XOk(XDocument(Reverse(acc)))
        Else
            If roots = 0 Then
                XErr("A DOCUMENT MUST HAVE A ROOT ELEMENT", i)
            Else
                XErr("A DOCUMENT MUST HAVE EXACTLY ONE ROOT ELEMENT", i)
    Else
        Select Case XNodeAt(s, i, d)
            Case XTBad(why, at)
                XErr(why, at)
            Case XTook(XText(t), n)
                If Not XIsBlank(t) Then
                    XErr("TEXT IS NOT ALLOWED OUTSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT", i)
                Else
                    XDocNodes(s, n, d, roots, Prepend(XText(t), acc))
            Case XTook(XElem(tag, attrs, kids), n)
                If roots > 0 Then
                    XErr("A DOCUMENT MUST HAVE EXACTLY ONE ROOT ELEMENT", i)
                Else
                    XDocNodes(s, n, d, roots + 1, Prepend(XElem(tag, attrs, kids), acc))
            Case XTook(v, n)
                XDocNodes(s, n, d, roots, Prepend(v, acc))
            Case Else
                XErr("UNEXPECTED END OF INPUT", i)

Rem ---- the public reader -----------------------------------------------

Def XmlReadDepth(s As String, maxDepth As Number) As XRead
    If XIsBlank(s) Then
        XErr("THE DOCUMENT IS EMPTY", 1)
    Else
        XDocNodes(s, 1, maxDepth, 0, { })

Def XmlRead(s As String) As XRead
    XmlReadDepth(s, XmlMaxDepth())

Def XmlParse(s As String) As Xml
    Select Case XmlRead(s)
        Case XOk(v)
            v
        Case XErr(why, at)
            Error("XMLPARSE: " & why & " AT " & Str(at))
        Case Else
            Error("XMLPARSE: UNREACHABLE")

Def XmlLoad(path As String) As Xml
    XmlParse(ReadFile(path))

Rem ======================================================================
Rem THE WRITER
Rem ======================================================================
Rem Never build a string with & in a left fold — that is quadratic in the
Rem output, which is exactly the shape of a serializer. Every writer word
Rem prepends FRAGMENTS onto an accumulator (so the list is built
Rem backwards, in constant time per fragment) and the join happens once,
Rem at the top, in XmlText and XmlPretty.

Def XmlText(x As Xml) As String
    Join(Reverse(XFrags(x, { })), "")

Def XFrags(x As Xml, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    Select Case x
        Case XDocument(ns)
            XFragList(ns, acc)
        Case XText(t)
            Prepend(XmlEscape(t), acc)
        Case XComment(b)
            Prepend("-->", Prepend(b, Prepend("<!--", acc)))
        Case XCData(r)
            Prepend("]]>", Prepend(r, Prepend("<![CDATA[", acc)))
        Case XDoctype(dtd)
            Prepend(">", Prepend(dtd, Prepend("<!DOCTYPE", acc)))
        Case XPI(t, dat)
            If dat = "" Then
                Prepend("?>", Prepend(t, Prepend("<?", acc)))
            Else
                Prepend("?>", Prepend(dat, Prepend(" ", Prepend(t, Prepend("<?", acc)))))
        Case XElem(tag, attrs, kids)
            If IsEmpty(kids) Then
                Prepend("/>", XFragAttrs(attrs, Prepend(tag, Prepend("<", acc))))
            Else
                XFragClose(tag, XFragList(kids, XFragOpen(tag, attrs, acc)))

Rem The two halves of a tag pair, so the nesting stays legible. Written
Rem as separate words rather than one long Prepend chain because that
Rem chain runs eight deep and a miscounted bracket in it is invisible.
Def XFragOpen(tag As String, attrs As List Of Pair, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    Prepend(">", XFragAttrs(attrs, Prepend(tag, Prepend("<", acc))))

Def XFragClose(tag As String, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    Prepend(">", Prepend(tag, Prepend("</", acc)))

Rem Note the If rather than Ifte throughout the writer. Ifte CALLS the
Rem branch it chooses, and a List is a quotation — so Ifte(done, acc, ...)
Rem would RUN the accumulator instead of returning it, scattering its
Rem fragments over the stack.
Def XFragList(xs As List Of Xml, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        acc
    Else
        XFragList(Rest(xs), XFrags(First(xs), acc))

Def XFragAttrs(attrs As List Of Pair, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    If IsEmpty(attrs) Then
        acc
    Else
        XFragAttrs(Rest(attrs), Prepend(XQt(), Prepend(XmlEscapeAttr(Snd(First(attrs))), Prepend("=" & XQt(), Prepend(Fst(First(attrs)), Prepend(" ", acc))))))

Def XmlSave(path As String, x As Xml)
    WriteFile(path, XmlText(x))

Rem ---- escaping --------------------------------------------------------
Rem & and < always, because they start markup. > as well: it is legal
Rem raw, but escaping it is what every other producer does, and it means
Rem a stray ]]> in text cannot be mistaken for the end of a section.

Def XmlEscape(s As String) As String
    Join(Reverse(XEscFrags(s, 1, 1, { }, False)), "")

Rem An attribute value additionally cannot carry the quote it is
Rem delimited by, and this writer always delimits with the double.
Def XmlEscapeAttr(s As String) As String
    Join(Reverse(XEscFrags(s, 1, 1, { }, True)), "")

Def XEscFrags(s As String, i As Number, run As Number, acc As List Of String, attr As Boolean) As List Of String
    If i > Len(s) Then
        XRun(s, run, i, acc)
    Else
        If XNeedsEsc(Mid(s, i, 1), attr) Then
            XEscFrags(s, i + 1, i + 1, Prepend(XEscOne(Mid(s, i, 1)), XRun(s, run, i, acc)), attr)
        Else
            XEscFrags(s, i + 1, run, acc, attr)

Def XNeedsEsc(c As String, attr As Boolean) As Boolean
    If c = "&" Or c = "<" Or c = ">" Then
        True
    Else
        attr And (c = XQt() Or c = Chr(9) Or c = XNl() Or c = Chr(13))

Def XEscOne(c As String) As String
    Select Case c
        Case "&"
            "&amp;"
        Case "<"
            "&lt;"
        Case ">"
            "&gt;"
        Case Else
            If c = XQt() Then
                "&quot;"
            Else
                "&#" & Str(Asc(c)) & ";"

Rem Turn the references in a string back into the text they stand for.
Rem The reader does this for you; this is here for text that arrived by
Rem another road.
Def XmlUnescape(s As String) As String
    Join(Reverse(XUnFrags(s, 1, 1, { })), "")

Def XUnFrags(s As String, i As Number, run As Number, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    If i > Len(s) Then
        XRun(s, run, i, acc)
    Else
        If Mid(s, i, 1) = "&" And XEntLen(s, i) > 0 Then
            XUnFrags(s, i + XEntLen(s, i), i + XEntLen(s, i), Prepend(XEntText(s, i), XRun(s, run, i, acc)))
        Else
            XUnFrags(s, i + 1, run, acc)

Rem ---- pretty ----------------------------------------------------------
Rem Only elements whose children are ALL elements are re-indented. The
Rem moment text and elements are siblings the content is mixed, and a
Rem line break inserted into mixed content changes what the document
Rem says — so mixed content goes out exactly as XmlText would write it.

Rem A pretty-printed DOCUMENT ends with a newline, because it is a file
Rem and files end with one. A pretty-printed element does not, because it
Rem is a value and you decide where it goes.
Def XmlPretty(x As Xml, indent As Number) As String
    If indent <= 0 Then
        XmlText(x)
    Else
        Select Case x
            Case XDocument(ns)
                Join(Reverse(XPFrags(x, indent, 0, { })), "") & XNl()
            Case Else
                Join(Reverse(XPFrags(x, indent, 0, { })), "")

Rem Content is mixed when text and markup are siblings, and that is the
Rem case a pretty printer must not touch: a line break inserted between
Rem <b>bold</b> and the word after it adds a space that was not there.
Rem Whitespace-only text between elements is NOT mixed content — it is
Rem the source's own indentation, and replacing it is the whole job.
Rem CDATA counts as text here whatever it holds. Its whole purpose is to
Rem carry characters that must survive exactly, so an element with a
Rem CDATA child is never re-indented — putting a newline and two spaces
Rem inside <recipe> would add them to the recipe.
Def XMixed(xs As List Of Xml) As Boolean
    Any(xs, Fn(k) => IsXCData(k) Or (IsXText(k) And Not XIsBlank(XChars(k))))

Def IsXCData(x As Xml) As Boolean
    Select Case x
        Case XCData(r)
            True
        Case Else
            False

Def XIsLayout(x As Xml) As Boolean
    IsXText(x) And XIsBlank(XChars(x))

Def XPFrags(x As Xml, indent As Number, level As Number, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    Select Case x
        Case XDocument(ns)
            XPDoc(ns, indent, acc, True)
        Case XElem(tag, attrs, kids)
            If IsEmpty(kids) Or XMixed(kids) Then
                XFrags(x, acc)
            Else
                XFragClose(tag, Prepend(XPad(indent, level), Prepend(XNl(), XPKids(Filter(kids, Fn(k) => Not XIsLayout(k)), indent, level + 1, XFragOpen(tag, attrs, acc)))))
        Case Else
            XFrags(x, acc)

Rem At the top level the whitespace between nodes is replaced with one
Rem newline apiece, which is what makes a pretty-printed document look
Rem like one rather than like its source.
Def XPDoc(ns As List Of Xml, indent As Number, acc As List Of String, lead As Boolean) As List Of String
    If IsEmpty(ns) Then
        acc
    Else
        Select Case First(ns)
            Case XText(t)
                XPDoc(Rest(ns), indent, acc, lead)
            Case Else
                If lead Then
                    XPDoc(Rest(ns), indent, XPFrags(First(ns), indent, 0, acc), False)
                Else
                    XPDoc(Rest(ns), indent, XPFrags(First(ns), indent, 0, Prepend(XNl(), acc)), False)

Def XPKids(xs As List Of Xml, indent As Number, level As Number, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        acc
    Else
        XPKids(Rest(xs), indent, level, XPFrags(First(xs), indent, level, Prepend(XPad(indent, level), Prepend(XNl(), acc))))

Def XPad(indent As Number, level As Number) As String
    StrRep(" ", indent * level)

Rem ---- canonical -------------------------------------------------------
Rem Sort is documented as ascending over all-numbers or all-strings, so
Rem it will not sort a List Of Pair by name. Sort the NAMES — a List Of
Rem String — and map them back through the attribute list to rebuild.

Def XmlCanonical(x As Xml) As Xml
    Select Case x
        Case XDocument(ns)
            XDocument(Map(ns, XmlCanonical))
        Case XElem(tag, attrs, kids)
            XElem(tag, Map(Sort(DictKeys(attrs)), Fn(k) => Pair(k, DictGet(attrs, k))), Map(kids, XmlCanonical))
        Case Else
            x

Rem ======================================================================
Rem NAVIGATION AND CONSTRUCTION
Rem ======================================================================
Rem XAttr, XHasAttr, XPutAttr, XDelAttr and XAttrNames delegate to
Rem dict.shoddy rather than reimplementing it: an element's attributes
Rem ARE an association list. The raw accessors XTag, XAttrs, XKids,
Rem XChars and the rest come free from the Type and abort on the wrong
Rem variant — they are the strict half of each guard pair, so they are
Rem not wrapped.

Def IsXElem(x As Xml) As Boolean
    Select Case x
        Case XElem(tag, attrs, kids)
            True
        Case Else
            False

Def IsXText(x As Xml) As Boolean
    Select Case x
        Case XText(t)
            True
        Case Else
            False

Rem The root element of a document, or the node itself if it is already
Rem an element — so XRoot(XRoot(d)) is XRoot(d) and a function that takes
Rem "a document or an element" can just call it.
Def XRoot(x As Xml) As Xml
    Select Case x
        Case XElem(tag, attrs, kids)
            x
        Case XDocument(ns)
            If IsEmpty(Filter(ns, IsXElem)) Then
                Error("XROOT: THE DOCUMENT HAS NO ROOT ELEMENT")
            Else
                First(Filter(ns, IsXElem))
        Case Else
            Error("XROOT: NOT A DOCUMENT OR AN ELEMENT")

Def XRootOr(x As Xml, dflt As Xml) As Xml
    Select Case x
        Case XElem(tag, attrs, kids)
            x
        Case XDocument(ns)
            If IsEmpty(Filter(ns, IsXElem)) Then
                dflt
            Else
                First(Filter(ns, IsXElem))
        Case Else
            dflt

Rem ---- attributes ------------------------------------------------------

Def XHasAttr(x As Xml, name As String) As Boolean
    Select Case x
        Case XElem(tag, attrs, kids)
            DictHas(attrs, name)
        Case Else
            False

Def XAttr(x As Xml, name As String) As String
    If XHasAttr(x, name) Then
        DictGet(XAttrs(x), name)
    Else
        Error("XATTR: NO ATTRIBUTE '" & name & "' ON <" & XTag(x) & ">")

Def XAttrOr(x As Xml, name As String, dflt As String) As String
    If XHasAttr(x, name) Then
        DictGet(XAttrs(x), name)
    Else
        dflt

Def XAttrNames(x As Xml) As List Of String
    DictKeys(XAttrs(x))

Rem An attribute read as a number, or the default if it is absent or is
Rem not one. Val is lax, so the text is checked before it is trusted.
Def XAttrNumOr(x As Xml, name As String, dflt As Number) As Number
    Let t = XTrimWs(XAttrOr(x, name, ""))
    If t = "" Or Not XLooksNumeric(t) Then
        dflt
    Else
        Val(t)

Def XLooksNumeric(t As String) As Boolean
    Let body = Ifte(Left(t, 1) = "-" Or Left(t, 1) = "+", Mid(t, 2, Len(t) - 1), t)
    If Len(body) = 0 Then
        False
    Else
        All(Map(Range(1, Len(body)), Fn(k) => Mid(body, k, 1)), Fn(c) => XIsDigit(c) Or c = ".")

Def XAttrBoolOr(x As Xml, name As String, dflt As Boolean) As Boolean
    BoolOr(XAttrOr(x, name, ""), dflt)

Rem ---- children and descendants ----------------------------------------

Rem Every child that is an element, in document order. The text, comments
Rem and CDATA are still there in XKids when you want them.
Def XElems(x As Xml) As List Of Xml
    Filter(XKids(x), IsXElem)

Def XCount(x As Xml) As Number
    Length(XKids(x))

Def XHasChild(x As Xml, tag As String) As Boolean
    Any(XElems(x), Fn(k) => XTag(k) = tag)

Def XChild(x As Xml, tag As String) As Xml
    If XHasChild(x, tag) Then
        First(Filter(XElems(x), Fn(k) => XTag(k) = tag))
    Else
        Error("XCHILD: <" & XTag(x) & "> HAS NO CHILD <" & tag & ">")

Def XChildOr(x As Xml, tag As String, dflt As Xml) As Xml
    If XHasChild(x, tag) Then
        First(Filter(XElems(x), Fn(k) => XTag(k) = tag))
    Else
        dflt

Def XChildren(x As Xml, tag As String) As List Of Xml
    Filter(XElems(x), Fn(k) => XTag(k) = tag)

Rem Every descendant element with this name, in document order, the
Rem element itself included if it matches.
Def XFindAll(x As Xml, tag As String) As List Of Xml
    Filter(XDescend(x, { }), Fn(k) => XTag(k) = tag)

Rem Every element in the tree, in document order. Built backwards and
Rem reversed once, as the writers are.
Def XDescend(x As Xml, acc As List Of Xml) As List Of Xml
    Reverse(XDescendR(x, acc))

Def XDescendR(x As Xml, acc As List Of Xml) As List Of Xml
    Select Case x
        Case XElem(tag, attrs, kids)
            XDescendList(kids, Prepend(x, acc))
        Case XDocument(ns)
            XDescendList(ns, acc)
        Case Else
            acc

Def XDescendList(xs As List Of Xml, acc As List Of Xml) As List Of Xml
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        acc
    Else
        XDescendList(Rest(xs), XDescendR(First(xs), acc))

Def XFind(x As Xml, tag As String) As Xml
    If IsEmpty(XFindAll(x, tag)) Then
        Error("XFIND: NO <" & tag & "> ANYWHERE IN THE TREE")
    Else
        First(XFindAll(x, tag))

Def XFindOr(x As Xml, tag As String, dflt As Xml) As Xml
    If IsEmpty(XFindAll(x, tag)) Then
        dflt
    Else
        First(XFindAll(x, tag))

Rem A path of child names, walked one step at a time. Not XPath the W3C
Rem language — child steps and nothing else.
Def XPath(x As Xml, path As List Of String) As Xml
    If IsEmpty(path) Then
        x
    Else
        XPath(XChild(x, First(path)), Rest(path))

Def XPathOr(x As Xml, path As List Of String, dflt As Xml) As Xml
    If IsEmpty(path) Then
        x
    Else
        If XHasChild(x, First(path)) Then
            XPathOr(XChild(x, First(path)), Rest(path), dflt)
        Else
            dflt

Rem ---- text ------------------------------------------------------------

Rem All the character data under a node, concatenated, with comments and
Rem processing instructions left out. CDATA counts as text, because that
Rem is what it is.
Def XTextOf(x As Xml) As String
    Join(Reverse(XTextFrags(x, { })), "")

Def XTextFrags(x As Xml, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    Select Case x
        Case XText(t)
            Prepend(t, acc)
        Case XCData(r)
            Prepend(r, acc)
        Case XElem(tag, attrs, kids)
            XTextFragList(kids, acc)
        Case XDocument(ns)
            XTextFragList(ns, acc)
        Case Else
            acc

Def XTextFragList(xs As List Of Xml, acc As List Of String) As List Of String
    If IsEmpty(xs) Then
        acc
    Else
        XTextFragList(Rest(xs), XTextFrags(First(xs), acc))

Def XTextNumOr(x As Xml, dflt As Number) As Number
    Let t = XTrimWs(XTextOf(x))
    If t = "" Or Not XLooksNumeric(t) Then
        dflt
    Else
        Val(t)

Rem ---- names -----------------------------------------------------------
Rem Namespaces are not resolved, so these two are how you look at a
Rem prefixed name without pretending to understand it.

Def XPrefix(name As String) As String
    If Instr(name, ":") = 0 Then
        ""
    Else
        Left(name, Instr(name, ":") - 1)

Def XLocal(name As String) As String
    If Instr(name, ":") = 0 Then
        name
    Else
        Mid(name, Instr(name, ":") + 1, Len(name))

Rem ---- functional update -----------------------------------------------

Def XPutAttr(x As Xml, name As String, val As String) As Xml
    XElem(XTag(x), DictPut(XAttrs(x), name, val), XKids(x))

Def XDelAttr(x As Xml, name As String) As Xml
    XElem(XTag(x), DictDel(XAttrs(x), name), XKids(x))

Def XSetKids(x As Xml, kids As List Of Xml) As Xml
    XElem(XTag(x), XAttrs(x), kids)

Def XAddKid(x As Xml, kid As Xml) As Xml
    XElem(XTag(x), XAttrs(x), Append(XKids(x), kid))

Rem The element with one text child, which is the shape of most leaves.
Def XSetText(x As Xml, t As String) As Xml
    XElem(XTag(x), XAttrs(x), { XText(t) })

Rem A leaf with no text is an EMPTY element, not one holding an empty
Rem text node — the two write differently (<b/> against <b></b>) and the
Rem first is what anyone building a tree by hand means.
Def XLeaf(tag As String, t As String) As Xml
    If t = "" Then
        XElem(tag, { }, { })
    Else
        XElem(tag, { }, { XText(t) })

Def XNode(tag As String, kids As List Of Xml) As Xml
    XElem(tag, { }, kids)

Rem ---- deep equality ---------------------------------------------------
Rem A List is a quotation and compares by identity, so = is only
Rem structural down to the first element. This is the comparison you want
Rem for a round trip. Attributes are unordered, as XML says they are;
Rem children are ordered, as XML says they are.

Def XEqual(a As Xml, b As Xml) As Boolean
    Select Case Pair(a, b)
        Case Pair(XElem(t1, a1, k1), XElem(t2, a2, k2))
            t1 = t2 And XAttrsEqual(a1, a2) And XKidsEqual(k1, k2)
        Case Pair(XDocument(n1), XDocument(n2))
            XKidsEqual(n1, n2)
        Case Else
            a = b

Def XAttrsEqual(a As List Of Pair, b As List Of Pair) As Boolean
    Length(a) = Length(b) And All(a, Fn(p) => DictHas(b, Fst(p)) And DictGet(b, Fst(p)) = Snd(p))

Def XKidsEqual(a As List Of Xml, b As List Of Xml) As Boolean
    Length(a) = Length(b) And All(Zip(a, b), Fn(p) => XEqual(Fst(p), Snd(p)))
